
 (NOTE : This is a copy of what is in the declaration section of
         the module )

 Direct Visual Basic Amiga Disk File Add-In Module (Phew!)
 ---------------------------------------------------------

    Version 0.99 - First Release - Early Janurary 1997

 Welcome to the first release of this add-on to make Visual Basic
 programmers (who make up a large percentage of hobbist programmers)
 a chance to use and get access to files and directories on ADF files.

 Because this is a first release DONT expect too much. It will allow
 you to look and move through a amiga disk file image without problems.
 Including sub-directories and files under that. All that is required
 is a form called FileListForm and three objects, two list boxes and a
 label. The first list box (for the directories) is called `List1` and
 list box two (for the files under that directory) is called `List2`.
 VB automatically gives the list boxes these names so don`t sorry
 about changing them. The Label MUST have its name changed to
 StatusLabel, as this reports the current position in the ADF file.
 Also, contained in this module is the code for handling a double-click
 on the directory list (list1), CUT the code out and paste it into the
 declarations part of the FileListForm as this will automatically place
 it in the List1_DblClick() routine. Also the Form_Load() code must
 also be CUT and pasted into the declarations section of the FileListForm.

 Changing the ADF file, is simple. Enter the Form_Load sub-routine and
 the first line reads Open "<FileName>" For Binary As 1 Len = 2, now
 all you have to do is change the file name.

 Exiting. When you exit your program (and therefore clode the DVB-ADF module)
 the ADF file is closed. I have not done this in the program because DVB-ADF
 needs to be able to use and `see` the file at all times. Closing it will
 crash the module.

 Error-Handling, is limited (infact nearly non-existant). This is
 because I have been using correctly put together ADF files. If you
 have a corrupt ADF file (or a demo/game adf file) and try and get
 this add-on to read it, well it will probably `Hang` - It hasn`t
 crashes, its just in an internal (eternal?) loop trying to make
 sense of the ADF file. You should take note about the following places
 * Closing a file when the module is using it. * Another program locking
 the ADF file when using it * Illegal values in root blocks (Ie. Values over
 decimal 1759) and other file/data blocks.

 Code, please don`t rely on the code for being correct. It's a simple
 beta version to see if I can get things to work! For example, the
 function called DecToHex is WRONG, not in its working but in its
 title, it should be HexToDec. I know its crap programming, but I have
 little time to worry about the `finer` points of programming. Anyway
 tidy my code, and mail it back to me and I will credit you!

 Other Things. This code was developed to allow a program called ADF-ZAP
 to find the start of files. This code also opens up another program
 that has been `stalled` called ADF Disk Manager. It will now be able
 to load and save MS-DOS files to ADF files directly.

